mike.lukas@gmail.com writes:

> reconsider.  One is that I don't think rsync does merging, which is a
> problem if player 1 starts a session, player 2 modifies the record file
> afterwards but before player 1 finishes, then player 1 leaves a score -
> player 2's score will be overwritten if the file is not merged.

The record file isn't kept open or in memory through the whole game, it
is read and updated when the game ends. It should be sufficient to lock
the file when one player's game starts reading it at the end and release
the lock when the update is finished.

